    <started></started>
    <completed></completed>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement FR-07 capture-side: make AI generation drift-proof. On Generate, drop a ProseMirror
    `Decoration` / `Selection.getBookmark()` at the user's current selection and tie it to the request id;
    as the user keeps typing during the generate window, rebase that bookmark through the concurrent edits
    using the op-log `Mapping` (task 022 / 020's rebased log). Pass the target `paraId` (the bookmark's
    resolved paragraph) to the model AS CONTEXT — the model returns JSON operations referencing paraId,
    NOT free text to text-search. On return, resolve the bookmark to its CURRENT position (post-concurrent-edit)
    so the returned operations land at the rebased selection, not the stale original offset.

    This is envelope-only. The engine is FROZEN (ADR-039): do NOT add a new AI dispatch endpoint and do NOT
    change any AI catalog row. AI dispatch goes through the existing `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` facade
    (ADR-013) — do NOT fork `Services/Ai/` and do NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`/executor/routing types anywhere.
    Reuse the EXISTING AI toolbar surface `widgets/ComposeAiToolbar.tsx` — do not build a new toolbar. Client
    fetches use `@spaarke/auth` (`useAuth`/`authenticatedFetch`) — no hand-rolled token handling (ADR-028).
    This is the R4 generate-window state-drift fix (design §5 AI paragraph, feature F5).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React/TypeScript engineer fluent in TipTap 3 / ProseMirror (Decorations, `Selection.getBookmark`,
    Step/StepMap/`Mapping` position rebasing) and the Spaarke AI facade contract. Understands that the
    editor is a lossy view + controller (I-6): the AI must be handed a stable `paraId` anchor and return
    ID-anchored operations, never free text the client would have to search for (violates I-7).
  </role>

  <goal>
    An AI generate flow where: a bookmark/Decoration is dropped at the selection on Generate and tied to the
    request id; the bookmark rebases through concurrent user edits via the op-log `Mapping`; the target
    `paraId` is sent as model context; the model returns JSON operations referencing paraId; and on return
    the bookmark resolves to its current position so operations land at the rebased selection. If the model
    returns free text instead of operations, the flow refuses and surfaces rather than text-searching.
    Wired into the existing `ComposeAiToolbar.tsx`; AI dispatch via the PublicContracts facade only.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5 (AI paragraph): "on Generate, drop a `Decoration`/`Selection.getBookmark()` at the selection,
      tie it to the request id, pass the target `paraId` as context. The model returns JSON operations
      referencing paraId (not free text to search). On return, rebase the bookmark to its current position,
      validate every returned paraId/offset against the live doc, then apply." Design §4 feature F5: the
      generate-window state-drift fix (NEW in R4). This task is the CAPTURE half (bookmark + resolve-on-return
      + paraId-as-context + refuse-free-text); the APPLY half (validate every returned anchor before apply;
      fuzzy-as-comment last resort) is task 041. Depends on 020's ProseMirror step→operation interceptor and
      its rebased op-log `Mapping` for the concurrent-edit rebasing. Gated on the Phase 0 gate (006).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeAiToolbar.tsx — the EXISTING AI toolbar surface; wire Generate to drop the bookmark/Decoration, tie it to the request id, and resolve-on-return</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/useAiGenerateBookmark.ts — NEW hook: create a Decoration/`Selection.getBookmark` at the selection tied to the request id; rebase through concurrent edits via the op-log Mapping; resolve to current position on return; expose the resolved paraId for model context</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/paraIdExtension.ts — TipTap schema carries `data-paraid`; resolve the bookmark's paragraph to its paraId via this</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/ — task 020 ProseMirror step→operation interceptor + task 022 rebased op-log `Mapping` (the position-rebasing primitive this reuses)</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ — the AI facade seam the generate call dispatches through (envelope-only; no new endpoint, no fork)</file>
      <file role="export">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/index.ts — export the hook if part of the public surface</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5 (AI paragraph), §4 F5 (generate-window drift fix)</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-07, Success Criterion 3</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">ProseMirror step→operation interceptor + rebased op-log `Mapping` — the position-rebasing primitive the bookmark reuses to survive concurrent edits.</dependency>
      <dependency task="006" status="pending">Phase 0 GATE — go/no-go for cutover; the operation schema (003) the model returns against is ratified here.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-07">On Generate a ProseMirror Decoration/bookmark is dropped at the selection, rebased through concurrent edits, and tied to the request id; the target paraId is sent to the model as context; the model returns JSON operations referencing paraId; on return the bookmark resolves to its current position. MUST NOT hand the model free text to text-search (invariant I-7).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039 / project">Engine FROZEN — MUST NOT add a new AI dispatch endpoint and MUST NOT change any AI catalog row. The AI redline path stays envelope-only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">AI dispatch goes through `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` only — MUST NOT fork `Services/Ai/`; MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`/executor/routing types into `Services/Compose/` or the client.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / project">Client generate/apply fetches use `@spaarke/auth` (`useAuth`/`authenticatedFetch`) — no hand-rolled token handling, no custom token props on the editor.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021 / project">All new/modified UI is Fluent UI v9 and MUST render correctly in dark mode (theme tokens; no hard-coded colors).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03 / project">Op capture + bookmark use RAW ProseMirror step/decoration/Mapping APIs on the MIT base — NO `@tiptap-pro/*`, no AGPL, no runtime dependency on EigenPal. Prefer zero new dependency.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Client component/unit tests exercise real editor state; NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests. (The automated concurrent-edit ProseMirror proof is task 042.)</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">New surface (the generate-window bookmark hook) — provide the `&lt;justification&gt;` (Existing / Extension / Cost-of-doing-nothing).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ProseMirror Decoration/bookmark + Mapping position rebasing; TipTap paraId resolution; AI facade envelope contract; Fluent v9 dark mode; BFF hygiene</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
