    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="paraId resolution from a position" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/paraIdExtension.ts">
        The schema carries `data-paraid` as a hidden node attr — resolve the bookmark's resolved position to its paragraph node and read its paraId to hand the model as context.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Rebased op-log Mapping" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/">
        Task 020/022 maintain an ordered, rebased operation log via ProseMirror `Mapping` — reuse the same Mapping to rebase the generate-window bookmark as the user keeps typing.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor (frontend + ai + docx; xhigh; opus). Load the knowledge files + design §5 + §4 F5. Read `ComposeAiToolbar.tsx`, `paraIdExtension.ts`, and task 020/022 op-log Mapping to understand how positions are rebased. State the Placement Justification (AI dispatch stays behind PublicContracts; no new endpoint; envelope-only).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Bookmark on Generate">In `useAiGenerateBookmark.ts`, on Generate drop a `Decoration`/`Selection.getBookmark()` at the current selection and tie it to the request id. Resolve the bookmark's paragraph to its paraId (via `paraIdExtension`) to hand the model as context.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Rebase through concurrent edits">Subscribe to editor transactions during the generate window; rebase the bookmark through concurrent user edits using the op-log `Mapping` (task 020/022) so it tracks the moving selection.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Dispatch with paraId context">Wire the Generate call through the existing AI facade (`Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`, via `@spaarke/auth`) passing the target paraId as context. Do NOT add a new endpoint. Instruct/parse so the model returns JSON operations referencing paraId.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Resolve-on-return + refuse free text">On return, resolve the bookmark to its CURRENT position and hand the returned JSON operations to the apply path (task 041) anchored at the rebased selection. If the model returns free text instead of operations, REFUSE and surface for review — do NOT text-search a placement (I-7). Fire the escalation trigger.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Wire into toolbar + tests">Wire the hook into `ComposeAiToolbar.tsx`; export from `index.ts` if public. Author component/unit tests (real editor state) for bookmark-drop, rebase-through-edit, and refuse-free-text, plus an ADR-021 dark-mode render check.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Verify + index">`npm run build:prod` the shared lib; run the new tests. Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>No existing generate-window bookmark. `ComposeAiToolbar.tsx` dispatches AI but has no concurrent-edit position tracking; task 020/022 maintain a rebased op-log `Mapping` for user edits but not a request-scoped selection bookmark.</existing>
    <extension>Cannot fold into the op-log interceptor (that captures user edits into operations, a distinct concern) nor into the toolbar (a dispatch surface). The generate-window bookmark is a cohesive request-scoped anchor with its own resolve-on-return lifecycle — a dedicated hook that REUSES the existing Mapping rather than a new position system.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, AI generation with concurrent user edits mis-places or fails — the returned operations land at the stale original offset, not where the moving selection ended up (the R4 generate-window drift defect). Concrete failing contract: FR-07 / Success Criterion 3 "generation with concurrent edits lands at the rebased selection" cannot be met.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The model returns FREE TEXT instead of JSON operations referencing paraId — do NOT text-search a placement (violates I-7). REFUSE, surface for review, and escalate per root §6 rather than improvising a text-anchor. Also escalate if honoring "operations referencing paraId" would require a new AI dispatch endpoint or an AI catalog change (ADR-039 conflict — surface as §6.5 Path A/B/C, do not silently add an endpoint).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/useAiGenerateBookmark.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeAiToolbar.tsx (bookmark drop + resolve-on-return wired)</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/useAiGenerateBookmark.test.ts</output>
    <output type="report">Placement Justification (AI via PublicContracts, no new endpoint, envelope-only) for the PR</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">On Generate, a Decoration/`Selection.getBookmark()` is dropped at the current selection and tied to the request id; the bookmark's paragraph paraId is resolved and sent to the model as context.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Generation with CONCURRENT user edits lands at the REBASED selection — the bookmark rebases through the concurrent edits via the op-log `Mapping` and resolves to its current position on return, not the stale original offset.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The returned payload is JSON operations referencing paraId (handed to the apply path 041); no free text is text-searched for placement.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: if the model returns free text instead of operations, the flow REFUSES and surfaces for review (fires the escalation trigger) — it does not silently place.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AI dispatch routes through `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` only — no new AI dispatch endpoint, no AI catalog change (ADR-039), no fork of `Services/Ai/`, no `IOpenAiClient`/executor/routing injection (ADR-013).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Client fetches use `@spaarke/auth`; no `@tiptap-pro/*` / AGPL / EigenPal runtime dependency added (NFR-03); ideally zero new dependency.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The toolbar/generate UI renders correctly in Fluent v9 dark mode (ADR-021); component tests pass; shared-lib `npm run build:prod` is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test name="Bookmark drops at selection on Generate">
      <steps>Select a phrase in a paragraph, click Generate on the AI toolbar.</steps>
      <expected>A Decoration/bookmark is placed at the selection tied to the request id; the paragraph's paraId is captured for model context.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Generation with concurrent edits lands at rebased selection">
      <steps>Select a phrase, click Generate, then keep typing elsewhere (and within the same paragraph) while the request is in flight; let the AI return operations.</steps>
      <expected>The returned operations land at the REBASED selection (bookmark resolved to its current position), not the stale original offset.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Free-text return is refused">
      <steps>Simulate the model returning free text instead of paraId-anchored operations.</steps>
      <expected>The flow refuses and surfaces for review; no text-search placement occurs.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Dark-mode render (ADR-021)">
      <steps>Render the AI toolbar + generate affordance under the Fluent v9 dark theme provider.</steps>
      <expected>Toolbar and any generate-state UI use theme tokens and are legible in dark mode; no hard-coded light colors.</expected>
    </ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>
    Capture half of FR-07; the apply/validate half (validate every returned anchor before apply; fuzzy-as-comment
    last resort) is task 041. Success Criterion 3 (AI drift-proof) is proven by the automated concurrent-edit
    ProseMirror test in task 042. Run `/conflict-check` before any BFF-touching PR (`Services/Compose/` +
    `Services/Ai/` overlap sibling projects).
  </notes>

